                <pb facs="0701" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv13/pg683"/>

                <head>Chapter II.—Rolling stock (Art. 370)</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 370.</p>
                <p>Germany undertakes that German wagons shall be fitted with apparatus allowing: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>of their inclusion in goods trains on the lines of such of the Allied
                            and Associated Powers as are parties to the Berne Convention of May 15,
                            1886, as modified on May 18, 1907, without hampering the action of the
                            continuous brake which may be adopted in such countries within ten years
                            of the coming into force of the present Treaty, and</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>of the acceptance of wagons of such countries in all goods trains on
                            the German lines.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>The rolling stock of the Allied and Associated Powers shall enjoy on the German
                    lines the same treatment as German rolling stock as regards movement, upkeep and
                    repairs.</p>
            </div>
